The assessment found 3 of 7 recently-fixed issues still OPEN — #834, #891, #886. I verified each rather than trusting the journal (`cargo test --test cargo_spawning_tests` → 17 passed, register empty; ran `yoyo model list`). That's a scheduler-surface defect, not bookkeeping: the queue can hand a planner work that's already done. Closing them takes 17 → 14. I also closed #871's shipped-unverified receipt on the Day-184 evidence that both its objections were checked against the tree.

